WEBVTT

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:11.400
You have to track dangerous animals, then get close to them without being attacked.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.880
It takes people with a very special mix of determination and dedication.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.000
Unbelievable!

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.800
Thousands try, but very few can do it.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:31.320
Now the BBC has chosen nine animal lovers from ordinary backgrounds to see if any of them has what it takes to become a wildlife film-maker.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:38.880
This week, the three remaining competitors battle it out in the final, in big-cat country.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.840
I'm really nervous now.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.320
They must master the art of filming the fastest and most powerful predators in Africa.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:57.600
One person will get a job with the BBC's Natural History Unit.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.480
For the winner, this will be their wildest dream come true.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:25.920
Its vast plains are home to many of Africa's most amazing animals, but it's most famous for its big cats and the prides of lions that make it one of the best wildlife locations in the world.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.840
Welcome to the final.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.480
And welcome to the Masai Mara.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.440
I'm well excited.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.880
I should hope you are well excited!

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:47.760
'I'm Nick Knowles, and I've been keeping an eye on the competitors 'as they're tried to prove they've got what it takes to win a job with the BBC's Natural History Unit.'

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.240
Look!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.240
That's a pocket-sized elephant.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:01.680
This is the final test for Cherylin, Anna and Allen.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:09.240
Over the weeks, they've been assessed by some of the world's most knowledgeable animal experts, led by film-maker James Honeyborne.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.960
He's been making award-winning wildlife programmes for the BBC for more than 20 years.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.640
He's the man our three finalists need to impress.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.120
I think filming in the Masai Mara is the ultimate wildlife filming test.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:31.720
Welcome to our bush camp, your home for these last five days.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.960
You're going to have to keep your wits about you to get through this week.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.200
Just three tents left.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.600
Pick one and get yourself settled in.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.360
It's pretty cool being in the Masai Mara.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.320
There's great wildlife.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.920
There's a... great big hippo walking behind me.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:03:02.440
Last week, the competitors aimed to book their place in the final by making a film about a conservation success story in just two days.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:08.240
Anna and Cherylin worked together and focused on the endangered black rhino.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.600
And they couldn't believe what was waiting for them.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.440
Oh, my goodness, look at that!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.880
Allen and Lucy were the other team and chose the rare Grevy's zebra as their subject.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.000
But some fascinating and ferocious lion behaviour stopped them in their tracks.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.880
Incredible!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.800
Awesome.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
What an amazing thing to see!

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:40.200
Anna and Cherylin kept searching for stories, and found out about a leopard capture and release from a local village.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.600
That was very cool.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:52.040
Lucy and Allen were sent to find cheetahs in a last-chance challenge.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.040
Emotionally, it's exhausting, and the thought of going home is horrible.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.640
I don't want to go home.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.000
And then James had to make his biggest decision so far.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.760
The person we're going to take through... ..is Allen.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.280
Allen had booked himself a place in the final.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.120
I know Cherylin wants this.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.040
She wants it badly.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.079
And I know Anna wants this.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.120
It's why we're all here.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:23.000
But I know one thing for sure - I want it more than them!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.400
I've said it all along.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.880
For the person who gets the job at the end of it, it's going to change their life for ever.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:38.720
It's home to massive amounts of wildlife.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.840
It hosts the biggest wildlife spectacle on the planet - the wildebeest migration.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:54.160
It's also hosted the BBC for over a decade, making the Big Cat Diary.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:06.480
They usually hunt as a team, meaning they can bring down prey far heavier than themselves.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.480
Then there's the world's fastest land mammal, the cheetah.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.920
They can accelerate from 0-70mph in just three seconds.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.400
On average, every other chase results in a kill.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:20.640
To get shots like these, taken by professionals, requires a good eye, a steady hand and nerves of steel.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:33.200
This week we're joined by a man who knows the Masai Mara inside out, Big Cat Diary presenter Jonathan Scott.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.120
I don't believe it!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.040
He's lived and worked in Kenya for decades.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:43.480
I can see by your smiles that you recognise our distinguished expert, so I'm sure you're very pleased that he's along with us for the week.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.520
Let me tell you about your final assignment.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:06:03.960
Each of you has to make a film... ..on the Masai Mara that's based around its most famous residents, the big cats.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:19.560
Each of you will have a day to direct a film, and each of you will be able to use your fellow aspiring film-makers in whatever role you see fit.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:24.160
And you have to choose a theme for your film - predator, survival, family.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:44.320
Because the BBC has made so many programmes here, film-makers can now recognise many of the big cats, and have even given names to those that have been featured regularly in series like Big Cat Diary.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:52.080
If you are just heading out that way, into the open, you're already in Marsh pride territory.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:57.360
You're also in the territory of Honey's boys, the three male cheetahs.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:05.360
If you were to go beyond them, you would be in Shakira's territory, with her three cubs.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.120
So as far as big cats are concerned, you are in the right place.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:14.560
Remember, you're in competition for the one big prize - a job with the Natural History Unit.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.200
We expect big things of you this week.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.840
'Each finalist will have one day to make their film.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:29.400
'They can use the other two competitors to help them, 'as camera operators, spotters or as researchers.'

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:37.720
James has decided that each finalist must make their film from footage shot on the day when they're in charge.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:43.000
He'll be assessing how each finalist performs then and, crucially, when they're working for the others, too.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.200
It's the toughest challenge they've faced.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.320
I'm really nervous now.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.480
I never get nervous, and I'm like...

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:59.200
This week, it's really pulling together everything that's happened before, so it's bringing together those skills, those experiences.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:02.960
They know the bush craft and the field skills, they know how to use a camera.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.960
They can make a good film.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:15.000
Cherylin will be taking charge tomorrow, and has already picked a theme for her film - family.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.160
I'm very interested in particular in cheetahs.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:21.400
My plan is to look at sibling bonding.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:28.560
But although Anna and Allen will be working for Cherylin tomorrow, she's chosen a surprising way of briefing her team.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.640
Right, then, guys.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:31.920
What I'm looking for is the interactions.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.799
Have you got a story in your head of what you want?

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:36.600
I have.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.960
Right.

00:08:36.039 --> 00:08:38.360
So...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:41.679
I'm not sharing that.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:44.880
I'll just use the initiative and...

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.960
I know that.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.920
I trust you 100%.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:49.720
Right.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:09:03.160
'At the end of the day, it's a competition,' and they don't need to know the story, because if I've asked them to follow a group of animals, and I want them to film the interactions, they can work it out for themselves.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:16.360
It's just after dawn in the Masai Mara, and Cherylin will have the whole day to make her film.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:21.800
Jonathan will be with her, too, assessing how she performs in an area he knows well.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.160
He'll then report back to James.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:31.960
Cherylin wants to make a film with the theme of family, and has sent 19-year-old Anna to track down the Marsh pride of lions.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.880
I'm going to see pussy cats!

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:47.480
Allen will hunt for the three cheetah brothers, while Cherylin herself will search the vast plains for the female cheetah, Shakira, and her cubs.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:10:00.440
You can't write her off, because you would have written her off in the first, second, third, fourth week, and here she is in the final, so who knows what she's capable of.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:06.160
39-year-old Cherylin has always been determined to change her life for the better.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.600
I was a manager in a fast-food restaurant and one day I thought, "Do you know what?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.680
"I don't care how much money I earn.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.960
"I'm going to give this up."

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.960
And I was offered a job working with animals and I took it.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.880
Now I'm a lecturer in wildlife and conservation, and I don't miss, "Do you want fries with that?"

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:29.520
And one of Cherylin's biggest fans is her sister, Lorna.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.280
Animals have been the main focus all her life.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.640
Her whole life, she's been working towards this, so to win it would be a dream come true.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:39.800
Over the weeks, her fighting spirit has kept her in the competition.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:46.800
She could have gone out in week two, week three, week four, but she kept bouncing back.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:51.880
When you really work with her and give her an opportunity, she rises to it and shines.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:56.440
Conquering fear of going in the water...

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.960
I've never been so scared in my life.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:02.440
..That was difficult.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.000
That's fantastic.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:07.640
But her biggest battle has always been with handling the camera.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.360
I am no good with technology.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:17.240
Press a button on a computer, I have to call the IT department to help.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.560
She's got a big hill to climb still.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:27.640
She's got nowhere to hide, she's on her own, she'll be driving a team to make the film she wants to make here, and she will be judged on that.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:40.360
She may be on a mission to find cheetah, but instead, Cherylin has stumbled upon lions from one of the biggest prides in the Mara, the Marsh pride.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.320
I'm having issues with technology.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.040
This could be a good starting point for her film about family.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:58.840
But to get close-up shots of the lions, she'll need a different lens, which means grappling with her old adversary, the camera.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:05.120
Sorry, I am wasting your time.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.880
'She was all over the place.'

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.960
I almost shook her at one point.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.320
You've been doing this for seven weeks.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.920
You should know how to put a lens on the camera.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:26.160
At first light, Cherylin sent Anna to film the Marsh pride and, luckily, she's turned up just in time.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.080
You go and find your one now!

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.560
The cubs have just joined them, Anna.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.120
OK?

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:36.520
I'm not technical, and I've done this about...three times, four times.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.720
And I'm like, "Argh!

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.840
Can't do it."

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.560
I hate it.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:43.520
I'm good at everything else.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:13:01.120
ANNA It's quite hard to believe that... we've been put smack, bang in the middle of the Masai Mara and we've got the chance to film lions, cheetahs and leopard.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.160
It's fantastic!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:12.560
While Cherylin continues her search for cheetah, Anna's left alone to film the pride, and they look like they might be on the hunt for breakfast.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:17.000
Between the ostrich and the lion, there's a little warthog.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:26.320
Cherylin's kept the theme of her film to herself, so Anna will have to use her judgment to get the best shots she can.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.480
Is that warthog safe now, Jacob?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.120
No, he's not safe, they're still waiting.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.080
Lions hunt together, slowly moving in for the kill.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:41.560
It's about to kick off.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.360
Look how close the warthog is.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.760
He's going to walk straight into her.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:07.120
Capturing a kill on camera is always a rewarding moment for a wildlife film-maker, and it would make a dramatic sequence for Cherylin's film.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.160
Look!

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:16.360
Missed it...didn't they?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:21.360
Lions will only keep up the chase for a while to conserve their energy.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.960
This warthog has avoided being breakfast.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.760
I wanted them to kill it!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:33.720
I think for Cherylin's film that will be very good.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.160
Very good footage.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:46.680
This whole area of nearly 1,000 square miles gets its name from the Masai people who live here.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:54.240
They herd their cattle in and around the national reserve, and have a complex relationship with the big cats.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:59.160
James and I are meeting up with a Masai called Harrison to learn more about life in the Mara.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:03.040
Am I right in thinking the tradition is that the great god you call Enkai...

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:04.920
Yes, Enkai.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:08.000
..He gave the Masai people all the cattle?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:12.040
Yeah, we believe that the Masai have descended from heaven with their animals.

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:17.200
And we believe that all animals on Earth, the cattle, belongs to the Masai.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:24.280
And is it true that because the cattle are so important to you, that you would give your life to defend your cattle from a lion?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.520
For sure, yes.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.240
Have you ever fought a lion?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.320
Sure, yes.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:32.920
We respect them and they also do respect us.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:36.960
It's only that when they come and attack our animals, we also attack them and kill them.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:40.560
So if there was a lion here, the safest place for me is here?

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:41.040
Yeah!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.280
THEY LAUGH Yeah!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:54.520
Anna's working hard for Cherylin and has remained with the Marsh pride.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:16:00.800
More lions have turned up, including a large male.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:11.480
This domestic spat will be great for a film about family.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:19.000
Everything that I wanted in my three-minute film has happened this morning, and I've shot all this for Cherylin and I can't use any of it.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.600
I'm very annoyed.

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:29.000
A few miles away, Allen's done just what Cherylin asked him to do.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:32.720
He's found the three cheetah brothers.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:40.080
We've got three cheetahs, actually...coming straight towards us at the moment.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:47.040
It's just wonderful, and it's amazing to be here doing this, when I think I could be sat at home.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.600
I can't fault it, really.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:59.680
But he hasn't been allowed in on the secret theme of Cherylin's film either, so he can't do any more than get good, clear shots of these beautiful animals.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:09.520
She's keeping her cards close to her chest, but I'm hoping if anything does happen of any interest, I can grab it and she'll be able to use whatever's of any interest to her.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:23.640
One of the most famous residents of the Mara is Shakira, a mother cheetah, who is a favourite of Jonathan Scott, who has spent many weeks filming her.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:28.599
Cherylin is determined to make Shakira the star of her film.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.680
Yeah, it's moving.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:30.920
Oh!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:40.640
The story of this cheetah could work well with Cherylin's family theme.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.280
She's had six cubs.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:47.720
Three have died, two possibly killed by lions, leaving three maturing females in her care.

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:51.200
My family, we're survivors, like those girls will be.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:58.440
Cherylin is from a big family, but she left home at 16.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:00.120
I've always had to fight for things.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.640
Coming from a house with lots of people in it, you've got to fight.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:05.120
"I don't want the last beans, excuse me, I'll get in there first."

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:07.440
We did come from a broken family.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:11.840
You do look out for everybody and you want to look after them.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:18.080
She's always remained close to her brothers and sisters.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:21.120
If you need her, she's always there.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.600
And she's someone you can talk to.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:26.680
If you've got a problem, you can go to her, and she'll be there for you, no matter what.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.080
Time's running out.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:41.720
But Cherylin manages to get lots more footage of the three cheetah sisters.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:51.240
My main thing was, if I found her, I wanted to talk about how females bond and males bond, and I've got three sisters here.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:53.680
So I'm going to watch the footage and see what happens.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:19:05.520
It's important for safety reasons that everyone gets back to camp before sunset, so Cherylin and her helpers today, Anna and Allen, head back.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:13.800
Cherylin will have to make her final film with the footage that everyone has shot today.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:17.760
I have huge respect for Cherylin.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.880
I mean, she is a tough cookie.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:26.440
She could have been crippled by some of the things that have happened to her on this journey, and yet she's dusted herself off, she's got back up.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:26.800
And you know why?

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.960
Because she believes in herself.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:37.640
Tomorrow, it will be Allen's turn to be in charge, with the other two finalists working for him.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:45.800
And in sharp contrast to Cherylin's approach, he decides to be very open about the theme of his film.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:50.520
Basically, what we're after tomorrow, the theme is going to be family.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:53.680
I haven't actually got a story yet.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:56.440
I'm hoping you'll shoot me something what I can build that around.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:20:02.880
So, er...showing how the family provides...baby-sitting, you know.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:06.520
Just think of these sort of things - how they communicate, especially with the cheetahs.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:11.400
If they've got cubs, there might be some communication there.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:16.800
Tomorrow's really important for me, to prove I'm a lot more than just a good cameraman.

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:22.160
I can see a story, I can develop a story and I can make a good film.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.400
That's what I'm really hoping for.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:29.440
It's dawn in the Mara and it's time for Allen to start his filming day.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:32.840
Jonathan will be watching him every step of the way.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.920
Yeah.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:50.160
You can't ask for a better morning than this to set the scene in.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.640
It's absolutely beautiful.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.760
I thought I'd be nervous, but I'm not.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.840
It's my moment.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.280
Despite his obvious love of nature, Allen's spent all his working life far from the great outdoors.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:11.000
Before heading to Africa, he was working nights in a warehouse.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:15.200
I mean, we all have to work and earn the wage.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:19.920
But I often dreamed that I'd be doing something else, something with nature.

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:29.320
Allen's the least travelled of all the competitors, and had never even been on a plane before.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:31.240
But he's coped with every challenge he's faced.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:39.480
He managed to keep filming killer bees, despite being stung as he wrestled with the ropes.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:48.720
He kept calm in a hot and humid cave as he searched for bats to film.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:56.840
His camera skills have constantly impressed us, and last week, he captured some of the most dramatic footage we've seen so far.

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:06.760
But Allen, who's more used to a solitary life and weekends photographing nature, has often struggled to stand up to team-mates, even when he's been right.

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:08.760
We can't walk away from that.

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:10.720
Got to do something with it.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:12.960
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:17.920
Very good call.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:28.120
'I want to see whether he can genuinely make an interesting film,' or whether he'll just go out and make films that have already been made before.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:30.760
I want him to step up to the mark and let his personality come through.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:33.680
In big cat territory, it's important to realise that there's potential danger everywhere.

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:35.600
Here's a question.

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:38.600
How come I can sit this close to a lion.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.240
?

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:41.480
I'm in an open-sided car.

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:44.120
The thing is, she can't see you.

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:46.400
She just knows, and she's known all her life, that cars are noisy.

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:49.520
They smell of diesel and rumble around.

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:50.200
But the silhouette's not human?

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:52.400
No.

00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:54.640
But if you were to stand on the roof, she'd go bonkers.

00:22:55.760 --> 00:22:56.920
If I stepped out here, same distance away?

00:22:55.960 --> 00:23:00.160
You'd give her a shock, and you don't want to do that.

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.560
That's stumbling into their world.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:06.200
Suddenly, they're confronted by you and it's fight or flight.

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:07.720
You wanted to get out and go to the loo, didn't you?

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:08.920
I think I'll hold it in.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.720
Sure?

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.160
Yes.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.720
Strong bladder.

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:10.840
OK, if you're sure.

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:20.000
Allen's been looking for lions too, but it's mid-morning and he still hasn't seen anything.

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:21.480
And there are more problems.

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:23.320
The jeep's engine's overheated and Allen's stuck.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:23.680
We're on fire here.

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:24.680
Smoke.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:33.520
Luckily, Jonathan's here to keep an eye on Allen.

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:33.840
Getting out of vehicles in the Mara isn't usually allowed.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:36.720
A big cat attack can come out of nowhere.

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:39.360
It's a little bit of a halt to the proceedings.

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:41.960
But we've no lions just yet.

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:47.160
I'm relying on the girls more than anything right now.

00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:59.120
When you're in the field, working in conditions like this, you're not in London, where you can just make a call and fix things, and you just have to adapt to the situation.

00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:03.160
Hi, Anna.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:04.360
How are you doing?

00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:05.720
I've found the three male cheetahs.

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:06.800
Wonderful.

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:09.760
'We're having a few problems here with the vehicle.'

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:16.320
So...you know, and we've not spotted any lions just yet.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:19.560
And Allen's problems are mounting.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.720
OK, we've got a lion, guys.

00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:27.040
Sorry to cut you short.

00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:28.800
Anna, just one second, please.

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:31.160
We're going from crisis management on the car.

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:31.920
We've got a lion coming.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:34.120
Right, Anna, you just carry on doing what you're doing.

00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:36.120
If anything changes, I'll let you know.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:37.800
But you're very good to keep going.

00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:46.400
The vehicle's ready to go again, and now Allen can focus on filming the lion who's been relaxing with her two cubs.

00:24:50.560 --> 00:24:52.080
Oh, look.

00:24:54.360 --> 00:24:55.920
It's absolutely... just perfect.

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:07.160
It's fantastic footage for his film and its theme of family.

00:25:06.280 --> 00:25:09.320
These cubs are around three months old.

00:25:08.560 --> 00:25:15.200
Even though lions have the highest survival rate of all the big cats, only around half will make it all the way to adulthood.

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:18.120
There's stories there.

00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:19.320
We just have to wait to see what happens.

00:25:24.760 --> 00:25:28.200
You're obviously very, very keen on wildlife.

00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:29.400
Yeah.

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.560
Is it your biggest passion?

00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:31.680
Wildlife?

00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:33.920
It's my only passion, really.

00:25:33.040 --> 00:25:34.880
What about girls?

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:36.000
Oh, yeah, girls...

00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:41.320
I mean, I don't have as much time for girls as I do wildlife, if that's what you're asking!

00:25:44.240 --> 00:25:51.160
Allen's spare time has always been taken up by wildlife, something his mum, Wendy, is only too aware of.

00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:57.360
I do worry about him and I do think he's lonely sometimes, being in the flat on his own, and I do wish sometimes he'd find himself a girl.

00:26:00.360 --> 00:26:04.160
I suppose a lack of confidence and shyness, stemming from being, you know, very little.

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:07.720
Being at school, I was bullied.

00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:12.440
So you'd rather just hide away and steer clear of people.

00:26:11.840 --> 00:26:17.640
I'm not shutting out the world and saying I don't want anybody, I don't need anybody, because I think we all do.

00:26:24.120 --> 00:26:27.320
When he was young, I bought him a camera.

00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:30.800
He'd take photographs and print them off, and then he'd draw the animals.

00:26:29.920 --> 00:26:32.520
I've got them all over the house, his paintings.

00:26:31.640 --> 00:26:40.240
I'm really proud of him.

00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:47.000
I can't just take one thing away from this.

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:47.400
I've got many things I'm taking away.

00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:51.320
The experience, the memories, the friends we've made.

00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:55.840
The whole journey has helped me come out of my shell.

00:26:54.880 --> 00:26:59.720
It means that I'm not going to hold myself back any more.

00:26:58.840 --> 00:27:02.120
That job is gold dust to me.

00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:05.120
I'd love to get it, and...

00:27:04.280 --> 00:27:08.080
It'd be true to say I don't want it to end.

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:09.920
I do not want to go home next week.

00:27:16.280 --> 00:27:20.080
Anna's been filming some male cheetahs for Allen all morning.

00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:22.840
But in the heat of the day, they are content to laze around in the sun.

00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:28.000
But Allen's other assistant for the day, Cherylin, is finding more success.

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:32.160
I have found Mrs Cheetah and her three ladies.

00:27:33.240 --> 00:27:37.160
It's Shakira, the female cheetah she filmed yesterday, with her three cubs.

00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:43.720
That was picture postcard, that was.

00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:52.520
This could be great footage for Allen, if Cherylin can focus and keep the camera steady.

00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:56.640
Got a cracking shot of the cub peeking out of the tree.

00:27:55.880 --> 00:27:59.400
It's like, whoa, wicked, because Allen will like that one.

00:28:03.040 --> 00:28:12.400
Allen's got a few great lion shots himself, but little else, and he'll be relying on Anna and Cherylin's footage if he's going to be able to put together a film that will impress James.

00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:16.640
I got the cubs up the tree.

00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:17.000
Oh, the cubs up the tree?

00:28:16.200 --> 00:28:18.320
One's peeking out, like that.

00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:18.560
"What you doin'?"

00:28:17.680 --> 00:28:22.520
I followed it, and I'm like that - "Oh, my life!"

00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:23.200
Cos it just went.

00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:30.160
But it turns out Cherylin's shots are very disappointing.

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:32.520
It's hard to say, but don't you think it's over-exposed?

00:28:33.320 --> 00:28:34.440
Er...

00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:35.040
Do you think they're usable?

00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:40.120
Cherylin's camera skills appear to have deserted her again.

00:28:39.800 --> 00:28:41.200
But this time, it's Allen who's going to suffer.

00:28:40.320 --> 00:28:44.880
Cherylin's not been so good with the camera as some of us.

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:48.200
I've seen what she got today, and she had a bit of a mare.

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:50.480
The action was there.

00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:54.160
You could see the animals, but you couldn't see the features really, really well.

00:28:53.200 --> 00:28:57.360
Everything wasn't 100% sharp.

00:28:56.560 --> 00:29:01.440
'He says, "Oh, you know, some of these, I can't use them."

00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:01.800
I felt a bit disheartened.

00:29:07.720 --> 00:29:12.720
Tomorrow, Anna will be in charge for the final filming day.

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:15.920
So far, Cherylin and Allen have used very different tactics.

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:19.480
Allen revealed his theme, which was family, which was quite helpful.

00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:23.560
If you know your director's theme, you can interpret it in your own way.

00:29:22.600 --> 00:29:28.240
Cherylin kept it very secretive and she's just given us a specific shot list.

00:29:27.400 --> 00:29:32.360
From the shot list, I was able to guess that she was doing family.

00:29:31.480 --> 00:29:37.240
But it would have been helpful for her to say, so that you can interpret things in a different way.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:43.000
As a result of Cherylin's difficulties with the camera, Allen's got less footage to work with.

00:29:42.920 --> 00:29:45.520
But he's staying upbeat.

00:29:46.280 --> 00:29:50.360
When I got out here, and it's the Masai Mara, what can you do but enjoy it, just go with it and really enjoy it?

00:29:51.840 --> 00:29:53.840
I think Allen's very deceptive.

00:29:53.400 --> 00:29:57.520
He could appear as if he was very shy, very quiet.

00:29:56.560 --> 00:29:58.520
I'm sure he is those things.

00:29:58.280 --> 00:30:05.680
But actually, if you turn the tap on, if you press the right button, there's a lot more there than you think.

00:30:04.840 --> 00:30:08.080
I find that very refreshing.

00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:09.520
I think he's got a lot of skill.

00:30:09.040 --> 00:30:11.040
Don't underestimate him.

00:30:17.440 --> 00:30:18.560
It's dawn.

00:30:17.640 --> 00:30:23.120
Anna, too, has chosen to make a film with the theme of family.

00:30:22.320 --> 00:30:28.600
She's making sure Cherylin and Allen know exactly what's expected of them.

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:32.240
She's clearly thought hard about how she should utilise her team-mates' talents.

00:30:31.400 --> 00:30:39.760
She's going to use Allen, the finalist with the best photographic skills, as her cameraman, and try to direct him.

00:30:38.800 --> 00:30:44.320
'It's a more intimate way of directing, 'being there with your team-mates, overseeing what they're doing.'

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:46.920
They'll work in the same vehicle.

00:30:46.200 --> 00:30:51.040
Anna's sent Cherylin in the opposite direction to try to find and film the cheetah brothers.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.720
She's the only one that's made a different call.

00:30:56.840 --> 00:30:58.160
Yeah.

00:30:58.280 --> 00:30:59.760
Two vehicles.

00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:01.920
Three cameras.

00:31:01.080 --> 00:31:02.880
She's going to direct them all the way through.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.120
Ambitious.

00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:13.040
It could be a clever move by the 19 year old, who's proved she's capable of holding her own with older competitors in Africa.

00:31:13.280 --> 00:31:16.320
Only two years ago, Anna was still at school.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:22.000
Then she took her first full-time job at Banham Zoo in Norfolk.

00:31:21.200 --> 00:31:25.080
Her mum, Kathleen, has always known about Anna's love of wildlife.

00:31:24.120 --> 00:31:30.760
She won't get out of bed to make anybody else a cup of tea or empty a dishwasher, but she'll get out of bed for an animal.

00:31:33.480 --> 00:31:38.720
But throughout this adventure, she's had to constantly push herself to stay in the competition.

00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:43.120
She was the only member of her team to get a dolphin encounter on film in Zanzibar.

00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:48.400
That's the best thing I've ever done in my life.

00:31:47.520 --> 00:31:50.480
She held her nerve to film a 12-foot crocodile in the springs of Mzima.

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:57.480
And she kept calm at the release of a leopard last week in Lewa.

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:08.560
Anna's the youngest, but showing a lot of promise.

00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:10.600
Very naturally in tune with the wildlife.

00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:11.840
And she's a good cameraperson.

00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:18.360
One question mark about Anna has been, can she direct a team.

00:32:17.480 --> 00:32:19.920
I think she likes to sit back and not be up front.

00:32:19.480 --> 00:32:24.320
This week, she's going to have to be up front and tell the others what she expects.

00:32:23.480 --> 00:32:28.920
She's found the Marsh pride of lions.

00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:30.520
It's her first chance to direct her cameraman for the day, Allen.

00:32:34.840 --> 00:32:37.240
There's some lions there.

00:32:36.960 --> 00:32:38.200
Whether there are...

00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:40.400
Jacob, can we head over that way, please?

00:32:39.560 --> 00:32:41.240
I think I've seen some of them.

00:32:40.440 --> 00:32:41.520
Look at them, they're just...

00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:53.560
That's what I want.

00:32:56.800 --> 00:33:04.680
The Marsh pride in all its glory is a stunning sight, and Anna's picked up a camera, too, to get the most out of this encounter.

00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:07.680
The family thing, the lions' social structure really fascinates me.

00:33:06.720 --> 00:33:08.840
Lovely backdrop, isn't it?

00:33:11.560 --> 00:33:19.880
A few miles away, Cherylin is on the hunt for the cheetah brothers.

00:33:20.880 --> 00:33:26.680
Her guide has heard on his radio they might be nearby.

00:33:28.920 --> 00:33:30.080
I have some lead also about the three boys.

00:33:29.120 --> 00:33:30.320
That's where I'm driving to now.

00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:30.880
You star.

00:33:30.080 --> 00:33:32.280
You are a private investigator.

00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:34.720
Yeah!

00:33:35.320 --> 00:33:37.200
FBI!

00:33:36.240 --> 00:33:37.880
FBI.

00:33:47.640 --> 00:33:53.840
But it looks like they've just missed a hunt, which would have been spectacular.

00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:54.280
Oh, they are even eating.

00:33:53.600 --> 00:33:56.400
A wildebeest kill.

00:33:55.760 --> 00:33:59.400
They just kill, I think we were just two minutes late.

00:34:02.360 --> 00:34:08.000
I've found the boys.

00:34:11.280 --> 00:34:19.920
James has told the finalists that he'll be judging them across all three days, whether they're in charge or not, so it's crucial that Cherylin gets some great footage here.

00:34:21.199 --> 00:34:26.760
I'm on the wide lens at the moment, which is nice.

00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:28.880
I could change it to the long lens, but I don't want to miss any action.

00:34:33.239 --> 00:34:35.560
Any time now, you could have the hyenas.

00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:39.960
And they will surrender kills to hyenas.

00:34:49.600 --> 00:34:53.239
The Marsh pride of lions are providing Anna and Allen with lots of material.

00:34:52.719 --> 00:34:54.960
Look at this now.

00:34:54.280 --> 00:35:00.320
They've caught a mongoose, and it's caused quite a stir amongst the family members.

00:35:03.320 --> 00:35:08.040
Five or six brothers fighting over a chocolate biscuit.

00:35:10.960 --> 00:35:12.800
Look, that one behind...

00:35:12.040 --> 00:35:13.360
It's gone in the hole.

00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:23.200
Anna seems totally focused on the job in hand, which hasn't always been the case at home.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:26.960
When she was 14 to 16, she was a classic teenager.

00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:27.920
I couldn't tell her anything.

00:35:27.120 --> 00:35:29.160
She didn't want to do her homework.

00:35:29.040 --> 00:35:33.520
I wouldn't say I'm like some hardcore rebel at home or anything.

00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:36.680
I'm just 19, to be honest.

00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:43.560
I remember work experience, she decided to go to the Raptor Foundation.

00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:44.080
I thought it was a cop-out.

00:35:43.120 --> 00:35:47.960
I thought it was just her having an easy time of it.

00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:54.000
I didn't realise until later, until I saw her at the centre, that the passion was growing.

00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:59.040
And it's this passion for wildlife that has made her so determined to do things her way.

00:35:58.080 --> 00:36:08.560
The reason I decided not to take my place at university is because, after working with the animals, I realised that I'm a lot better in that field as opposed to an academic point of view.

00:36:13.320 --> 00:36:17.720
She thinks that I believe she should be sitting behind a desk.

00:36:16.880 --> 00:36:18.640
I actually do not want that for Anna.

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:21.880
I want her to be fulfilling her potential.

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:32.040
I know that, no matter where I go from here, my whole life's career is going to be something around animals.

00:36:31.080 --> 00:36:34.120
Because that's what I love and what I'm good at.

00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:38.080
Anna's filming day is nearly over.

00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:44.240
Tomorrow, the three finalists will find out who will get the job with the BBC's Natural History Unit.

00:36:50.840 --> 00:36:53.400
Hippopotamus crossing the road here.

00:36:54.440 --> 00:36:59.040
Every day, there's something new and different.

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:02.240
Today has been fab.

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:05.560
I've got some fantastic footage.

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:08.840
Allen and Cherylin worked fantastically for me today.

00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:08.960
They've got all the shots I wanted.

00:37:08.120 --> 00:37:10.440
I couldn't be happier with what I've got.

00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:15.960
About 24 hours left until we have to make the decision.

00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:17.560
And it's not a foregone conclusion at this stage at all.

00:37:27.600 --> 00:37:32.480
For Cherylin, Allen and Anna, this is the day of reckoning.

00:37:35.360 --> 00:37:37.760
Hi, I'm Dan.

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:45.720
With the help of an editor, they must get the best out of their footage, write a script and prove to James they have the potential to be wildlife film-makers.

00:37:50.080 --> 00:37:54.680
Allen had the least amount of footage from his day's filming.

00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:56.560
Will he have enough to produce a winning film?

00:37:56.280 --> 00:38:01.000
Can I have a look at the next shot before I make a decision?

00:38:00.240 --> 00:38:03.400
I'm just wondering if any of it's going to work at the moment.

00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:08.560
Natural history is my passion.

00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:11.400
Whether it be photographing, filming, painting.

00:38:10.440 --> 00:38:19.520
I believe I've got enough talent and belief now to really go for it, and realise them dreams.

00:38:18.720 --> 00:38:20.040
I think they're seeing the real me.

00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:25.320
And I think I'm seeing the real me as well.

00:38:24.600 --> 00:38:27.560
Cherylin struggled with the camera on her day.

00:38:26.760 --> 00:38:31.960
But luckily, Anna got her some great footage of lions.

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:32.320
One cheetah walking through the grass long.

00:38:31.560 --> 00:38:32.720
One cheetah walking behind another.

00:38:34.200 --> 00:38:35.720
There.

00:38:34.760 --> 00:38:41.240
Will she stick to her cheetah story or change it to include Anna's footage?

00:38:40.360 --> 00:38:46.320
Although they look docile and placid, lions are always alert.

00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:48.520
Anna used different tactics, choosing two cameras filming one pride of lions, and left Cherylin to film on her own.

00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:56.560
But was it the right decision?

00:38:55.840 --> 00:38:58.400
I'd love to get the job over Cherylin and Allen.

00:38:57.560 --> 00:39:03.440
Although I'm younger, perhaps I've got more energy, a different outlook on things that older people wouldn't have.

00:39:02.920 --> 00:39:05.000
But, you know, there's loads of stuff I don't know.

00:39:04.240 --> 00:39:07.160
I've only had 19 years of life.

00:39:06.360 --> 00:39:09.320
There's lots I'm going to have to be taught.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:14.080
In Cherylin's edit, the pressure is getting to her.

00:39:15.640 --> 00:39:17.360
Can't find it.

00:39:16.520 --> 00:39:17.960
It's not on there.

00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:19.720
003245.

00:39:18.840 --> 00:39:20.960
It's not on there.

00:39:20.640 --> 00:39:22.600
How many minutes have I got left on the film?

00:39:21.680 --> 00:39:24.120
You're at 45 seconds to go.

00:39:23.240 --> 00:39:24.360
45 seconds to go.

00:39:23.400 --> 00:39:26.040
That's quite a way.

00:39:25.400 --> 00:39:26.560
It is.

00:39:25.760 --> 00:39:27.320
Ten minutes left.

00:39:26.720 --> 00:39:29.360
I know.

00:39:28.560 --> 00:39:34.400
And her editor Dan is surprised by the footage she's chosen for her film.

00:39:33.520 --> 00:39:36.840
She's got a lot of stuff that she picked out in her initial selects that she's not used.

00:39:36.080 --> 00:39:39.240
It's too dark, which is her camerawork.

00:39:41.160 --> 00:39:43.640
It was crap, that.

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:45.920
She was completely lost.

00:39:45.040 --> 00:39:47.040
She was a bit at sea.

00:39:46.080 --> 00:39:47.280
No worries.

00:39:46.320 --> 00:39:47.840
Take care.

00:39:56.360 --> 00:40:01.040
What's got you in a state now?

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:06.680
You know when you just want it to be just right?

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:09.680
Just for once, just right...

00:40:09.640 --> 00:40:12.960
You haven't thrown in the towel, have you?

00:40:12.600 --> 00:40:16.080
Excuse me, you know I never throw in the towel.

00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:18.560
You managed a burger place for years, yeah?

00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:19.840
Yeah.

00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:21.720
And then decided you were going to completely change your life.

00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:22.440
Yeah.

00:40:21.720 --> 00:40:23.920
How many people do that?

00:40:23.120 --> 00:40:24.400
Not that many.

00:40:23.680 --> 00:40:25.040
Right.

00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:29.240
Then you turn up on this, thinking you haven't got a chance, and, week on week, you manage to pull it off.

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:31.200
Yeah, I know.

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:34.280
But that's what I'm like, innit?

00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:35.760
I'm that sort of person.

00:40:35.160 --> 00:40:38.040
You're a fighter.

00:40:37.480 --> 00:40:40.000
I know I am.

00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:40.760
So be proud of it.

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:41.360
I am.

00:40:40.400 --> 00:40:42.440
And fight.

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.280
I am proud of that.

00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:44.560
Like a cheetah.

00:40:51.840 --> 00:40:58.400
It was only two months ago, nine British wildlife enthusiasts began a crash course in film-making.

00:40:57.960 --> 00:41:11.000
Across the amazing continent of Africa, from swamp to desert, mountains to the deep blue sea, searching out and filming incredible wildlife.

00:41:14.760 --> 00:41:23.400
For one of them, their wildest dream is about to come true - a job at the world-renowned Natural History Unit.

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:29.520
This week, there's no last chance challenge.

00:41:28.720 --> 00:41:35.960
They will be judged on their final film and how they've progressed during their time in Africa.

00:41:37.280 --> 00:41:40.520
This, of course, was your last great assignment.

00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:42.440
So, we are going to start with Cherylin's.

00:41:41.920 --> 00:41:43.520
Ready?

00:41:43.280 --> 00:41:44.360
Yeah.

00:41:43.520 --> 00:41:45.160
Let's take a look.

00:41:45.360 --> 00:41:48.440
Cherylin's film is called Unbreakable.

00:41:52.520 --> 00:41:57.480
'Cats - majestic creatures.

00:41:56.920 --> 00:41:58.400
'Born predators.

00:41:57.560 --> 00:41:59.720
The kings and queens of animals.

00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:03.240
'So how have they become so successful?

00:42:02.960 --> 00:42:05.040
'How have they earned this status?

00:42:04.080 --> 00:42:11.360
'Here in the Masai Mara, in Kenya, it's all about teamwork.

00:42:10.840 --> 00:42:17.600
'One family of cats has to work much harder as a team in their early years than others.

00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:24.680
'This cat is the cheetah.

00:42:23.840 --> 00:42:25.320
'Quite often, you will see groups of related males.

00:42:25.040 --> 00:42:32.000
'By having brothers and sisters, they can hunt more efficiently and kill more often.

00:42:31.080 --> 00:42:38.200
'So, it is sure to say that family bonds and working together is a real recipe for survival.

00:42:37.320 --> 00:42:39.440
'Well, it works in the Masai Mara, doesn't it?'

00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:48.080
Now, it goes without saying that we think you've come a long way.

00:42:47.480 --> 00:42:54.120
From this point on, though, we want to break down the films, so we would appreciate you being straightforward and honest about how you've done that.

00:42:55.240 --> 00:42:58.720
There were a couple of cheetah shots in there which were quite dark.

00:42:58.080 --> 00:43:00.000
Yes.

00:42:59.120 --> 00:43:01.600
Was that part of the camera trouble you said you had?

00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:02.200
Yes, it was.

00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:03.760
What happened?

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:05.800
It was my exposure.

00:43:05.080 --> 00:43:09.840
A few weeks ago you said you were going to go to bed and read the manual.

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:09.960
Yeah, I know.

00:43:09.000 --> 00:43:10.800
And then...

00:43:10.040 --> 00:43:11.240
Did you?

00:43:10.440 --> 00:43:11.840
No.

00:43:14.240 --> 00:43:18.240
Anna shot you some extraordinary stuff of the lions.

00:43:18.080 --> 00:43:19.680
Yes, I know she did.

00:43:18.880 --> 00:43:20.760
But you stuck with the cheetahs.

00:43:20.080 --> 00:43:21.840
Why?

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:28.240
I did stick with the cheetahs because I just thought that was a different sort of relationship.

00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:32.880
Did you talk about your theme to your team-mate?

00:43:31.920 --> 00:43:34.720
Not really, no.

00:43:34.520 --> 00:43:38.520
I think they knew that I was doing "family".

00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:41.520
Would it have helped you in your choice of shots had you known?

00:43:40.560 --> 00:43:47.720
Yeah, definitely would have helped to know more about it.

00:43:47.800 --> 00:43:50.880
I really liked my story.

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:59.800
Allen, shall we take a look at your film?

00:43:58.960 --> 00:44:00.240
Yes, please.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:04.680
Allen has called his film Without A Pride.

00:44:03.960 --> 00:44:08.840
'This is the Masai Mara.

00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:12.560
'Its endless plains play host to many herbivores.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:18.120
'This, of course, means the Mara is rich in carnivores and is famed for its big cats.

00:44:18.880 --> 00:44:21.520
'This is one of many lion prides that dwell here.

00:44:21.000 --> 00:44:24.480
'Hiding in the cover is their sister.

00:44:24.480 --> 00:44:28.600
'She has two three-month-old cubs.

00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:35.680
'For the first few months of their lives, she will raise them alone.

00:44:35.360 --> 00:44:42.160
'A group of unrelated females have been drawn in by the vast numbers of wildebeests.

00:44:43.120 --> 00:44:51.720
'But unknown to the young family, they are literally just 200 metres away.

00:44:50.840 --> 00:44:59.280
'Should the two young families meet, the outcome could be disastrous - especially for the cubs.

00:44:58.320 --> 00:45:03.920
'Outnumbered, will the young mother be able to fend them off 'or will her sisters come to her aid?'

00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:12.360
Allen, is that a final-winning film?

00:45:14.360 --> 00:45:15.960
I hope so.

00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:19.720
I feel I made the most of what I got.

00:45:19.040 --> 00:45:21.760
And how was Cherylin's footage?

00:45:21.200 --> 00:45:25.640
It was dark, as Cherylin explained with her footage.

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:27.600
Did you tell Cherylin that her footage was unusable?

00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:29.120
Yeah.

00:45:31.240 --> 00:45:33.800
Were you surprised that you were that assertive?

00:45:32.960 --> 00:45:37.320
I probably surprised a lot more people than myself, actually.

00:45:36.480 --> 00:45:37.760
I know I can do it.

00:45:41.400 --> 00:45:42.880
Thank you very much.

00:45:42.040 --> 00:45:44.600
Two films down, one to go.

00:45:43.720 --> 00:45:45.800
Anna, let's take a look at your film.

00:45:51.040 --> 00:45:56.000
Anna's film is titled Family Strengths.

00:45:55.960 --> 00:46:02.080
'The Masai Mara, famous for its big cats.

00:46:01.560 --> 00:46:05.120
'The most successful big cats are the lions.

00:46:04.440 --> 00:46:11.160
'This pride consists of four females, nine cubs and two large males.

00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:16.200
'Although they look docile and placid, lions are always alert.

00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:27.880
'Because they stick together as a family, there are many eyes to watch for danger, 'more bodies to defend territory and more weapons to hunt for larger food like zebra or wildebeest.

00:46:31.360 --> 00:46:36.880
'Although larger prey feeds more mouths, small mammals offer perfect hunting practice.

00:46:36.920 --> 00:46:47.840
'In the Mara, where food is plentiful, and as long as family bonds are strong and true, 'these beautiful cats could continue to thrive for generations to come.'

00:46:50.280 --> 00:46:53.600
Do you feel you got the best out of your team?

00:46:53.680 --> 00:46:55.160
I do, yes.

00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:55.280
I enjoyed the responsibility.

00:46:54.400 --> 00:46:57.960
I did really enjoy directing this week.

00:46:57.720 --> 00:47:00.800
They came back with some amazing footage and they did exactly what I asked of them.

00:46:59.880 --> 00:47:04.040
The first day was really frustrating for you.

00:47:03.080 --> 00:47:04.640
Wasn't it?

00:47:04.520 --> 00:47:06.640
Yeah, it was.

00:47:05.720 --> 00:47:10.800
I would have loved to have used the footage I shot for Cherylin on first day.

00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:16.040
I gave my total best to these two because, in order to get the best out of them, I've got to give the best...

00:47:15.120 --> 00:47:16.640
It works both ways.

00:47:17.920 --> 00:47:22.440
At the beginning of the day, you went out with two cameras in one vehicle.

00:47:22.440 --> 00:47:24.000
Mm-hm.

00:47:23.040 --> 00:47:24.160
What was the reasoning behind that?

00:47:24.360 --> 00:47:27.160
It actually worked out quite well.

00:47:26.320 --> 00:47:32.120
Allen was on the tight with the long lens and I was shooting wide beside him.

00:47:31.960 --> 00:47:36.040
It worked out well.

00:47:35.080 --> 00:47:37.600
Allen, do you feel that worked out well?

00:47:36.680 --> 00:47:39.240
From what I did, I wanted to find a story.

00:47:38.400 --> 00:47:45.560
I felt sending us all out separately to cover more ground and more cats had the better chance of finding that.

00:47:44.720 --> 00:47:47.440
But you know, it's your decision at the end of the day.

00:47:51.400 --> 00:47:57.680
You should be proud of the films you made and what you learned over the last eight, nine weeks.

00:47:56.880 --> 00:47:59.640
Here you are, and you deserve your place in the final.

00:47:59.720 --> 00:48:03.360
The question for us now is trying to split that.

00:48:03.960 --> 00:48:12.720
Now we've seen their films, each finalist has one last chance to convince James they're the one for the job.

00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:14.400
First, it's Cherylin.

00:48:13.480 --> 00:48:17.400
Is her fighting spirit enough to win the prize?

00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:18.160
Why do you want to do this job?

00:48:17.200 --> 00:48:19.840
What's so important about this job?

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:24.640
I work in education now, and I can tell this amount of people about stuff.

00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:28.240
But if I work in television, I can tell that amount of people about stuff.

00:48:27.560 --> 00:48:32.160
This is the time to change that career and move it up a step.

00:48:31.280 --> 00:48:33.360
It's been tough for you, hasn't it?

00:48:32.400 --> 00:48:35.120
Yeah, it has.

00:48:34.160 --> 00:48:38.200
God, how many times have I cried?

00:48:37.240 --> 00:48:38.440
Quite a lot.

00:48:37.600 --> 00:48:43.240
It has been tough, but I always manage to go, "No, you know what?

00:48:43.240 --> 00:48:45.920
"I can do this and I will do this."

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:46.440
That's why I am sat here.

00:48:47.560 --> 00:48:49.160
Here's my problem.

00:48:48.240 --> 00:48:58.480
I'm not sure that any team can afford to have a player on board that you have to keep picking up and encouraging, and picking up and encouraging.

00:48:57.640 --> 00:49:02.120
If I'm in a job, I'm not going to be stood there squawking like a baby.

00:49:01.240 --> 00:49:04.880
Yes, I have battled through this and picked myself up.

00:49:03.920 --> 00:49:05.840
But I am a very determined lady.

00:49:05.640 --> 00:49:07.640
I've got really good skills.

00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:10.600
And that's why I should win.

00:49:17.040 --> 00:49:18.480
OK, Cherylin, thank you very much.

00:49:19.040 --> 00:49:26.160
With a storm brewing, it's Allen's turn next.

00:49:25.240 --> 00:49:32.760
His camerawork and natural instincts have always impressed, but his ability to lead and stand up for himself has caused concern.

00:49:32.480 --> 00:49:34.080
Your strengths.

00:49:34.160 --> 00:49:37.040
What are those?

00:49:36.640 --> 00:49:38.400
Er...

00:49:37.440 --> 00:49:40.640
You know, passion.

00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:42.160
I love what I do.

00:49:41.800 --> 00:49:44.920
Can you speak up a bit, please, Allen?

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:45.760
Sorry, yeah.

00:49:44.800 --> 00:49:48.800
Obviously the camerawork and the willingness to learn.

00:49:49.160 --> 00:49:52.840
I could barely hear you over the storm.

00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:57.520
How am I going to hear you in a briefing or when I'm trying to get information back from a team when they're going out filming?

00:49:57.240 --> 00:49:59.760
You'll have to sit closer!

00:49:58.800 --> 00:50:00.000
Sorry...

00:49:59.200 --> 00:50:01.360
No, I'm serious.

00:50:00.640 --> 00:50:02.920
This is a major problem.

00:50:02.200 --> 00:50:04.680
Also, your answers very often tend to waffle on a bit.

00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:05.040
You're aware of that, presumably?

00:50:04.120 --> 00:50:05.520
Yes.

00:50:04.640 --> 00:50:07.000
Definitely.

00:50:08.960 --> 00:50:11.200
Do you think that something you can curb as well?

00:50:11.120 --> 00:50:13.280
Yes.

00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:17.000
Why should you win this?

00:50:16.040 --> 00:50:21.680
I still don't think there's anybody in this competition wants this more than I do.

00:50:23.600 --> 00:50:26.800
Why, because you don't want to go back to your previous life?

00:50:26.320 --> 00:50:29.400
No, I definitely don't want to go back there.

00:50:28.640 --> 00:50:35.120
I do believe that, whatever the outcome today, my life's gonna change.

00:50:36.600 --> 00:50:41.240
Is your ultimate goal to film and direct your own films?

00:50:40.520 --> 00:50:42.000
Yes.

00:50:41.160 --> 00:50:42.920
Definitely.

00:50:45.200 --> 00:50:48.600
To do that, what's the best next step for you?

00:50:48.840 --> 00:50:50.160
Winning this.

00:50:49.280 --> 00:50:50.840
Good luck, Allen.

00:51:01.520 --> 00:51:08.560
The youngest competitor, Anna, only emerged as a potential finalist in the last few weeks.

00:51:07.720 --> 00:51:09.920
Has she left it too late to prove she's a winner?

00:51:10.560 --> 00:51:13.040
Passion.

00:51:12.200 --> 00:51:16.240
Do you have that single-mindedness?

00:51:15.360 --> 00:51:18.920
Is this really what you want to do with your life?

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:19.560
It is something that I really want.

00:51:18.680 --> 00:51:22.240
Wildlife absolutely fascinates me.

00:51:21.640 --> 00:51:24.640
It's been a passion of mine from a very young age.

00:51:23.880 --> 00:51:27.600
Your youth could be a plus or a minus.

00:51:26.720 --> 00:51:31.440
I believe my opinion is just as valid as anybody older or younger than me.

00:51:30.480 --> 00:51:36.800
My skills and my love lie in actually working with animals hands-on.

00:51:36.040 --> 00:51:38.280
Why should you win this?

00:51:37.400 --> 00:51:41.080
Because I'm a very passionate about my animals.

00:51:41.040 --> 00:51:44.840
You don't have to tell me anything twice.

00:51:44.080 --> 00:51:45.600
I'm quite knowledgeable about a lot of animals.

00:51:44.840 --> 00:51:46.320
Thank you very much.

00:51:53.400 --> 00:51:56.080
Well done, guys, well done.

00:51:55.200 --> 00:51:58.880
It doesn't matter now, does it, whoever wins?

00:51:57.920 --> 00:51:59.080
No.

00:51:58.200 --> 00:52:05.680
The relief of having your one-on-one grilling is over, but the tenterhooks of the final decision are always terrible.

00:52:04.720 --> 00:52:07.120
We hate them.

00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:09.080
There's nothing more we can do.

00:52:08.200 --> 00:52:11.760
It's in James' hands now.

00:52:19.160 --> 00:52:23.800
I'll tell you what, they've all come a long way, haven't they?

00:52:23.080 --> 00:52:25.920
Three great films.

00:52:24.960 --> 00:52:26.280
I really enjoyed all three of them.

00:52:25.720 --> 00:52:26.840
I have to say that first and foremost.

00:52:26.160 --> 00:52:30.160
I really enjoyed all three, and very different.

00:52:29.280 --> 00:52:32.600
That's the most interesting film Allen's made, don't you think?

00:52:31.760 --> 00:52:34.480
I think probably the best of the three.

00:52:33.720 --> 00:52:35.560
You think his is the best of the three?

00:52:35.080 --> 00:52:37.440
I'll tell you why.

00:52:36.640 --> 00:52:38.440
He had the least...

00:52:37.760 --> 00:52:42.000
The least stuff, behaviour-wise, in there.

00:52:41.840 --> 00:52:42.920
But he really drove a story.

00:52:43.080 --> 00:52:46.640
What I love is I think he's actually surprised himself.

00:52:45.840 --> 00:52:48.520
Yes.

00:52:48.400 --> 00:52:55.560
I'm here in the final and I've been in situations where they could have sent me home and I've done badly.

00:52:54.600 --> 00:52:56.440
And they've kept me in.

00:52:55.480 --> 00:52:58.640
I'm here to win and I can do it.

00:53:01.440 --> 00:53:06.280
Cherylin, she's done so well, she's full of courage.

00:53:05.320 --> 00:53:07.480
She's very personable.

00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:09.160
She's great at getting something out of people.

00:53:08.200 --> 00:53:09.720
And she's very organised.

00:53:08.760 --> 00:53:13.520
Her logistical skills around those exercises were very good.

00:53:14.360 --> 00:53:17.920
When I heard her voice, I thought, "Hang on, I don't know this person."

00:53:17.200 --> 00:53:19.040
It was a lovely voice.

00:53:19.320 --> 00:53:24.640
She's got weaknesses but she's got huge strengths too.

00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:28.880
If I'm the woman for the job, they've got to take it, warts and all.

00:53:29.920 --> 00:53:32.400
Anna's film I really liked.

00:53:31.600 --> 00:53:37.680
I suddenly understood the Masai Mara at the beginning of her film and then she went on to tell a story, don't you think?

00:53:36.760 --> 00:53:44.800
Each of the three people that you've whittled down into the final have attributes that would, together, make you a perfect person.

00:53:43.920 --> 00:53:49.920
Cherylin, I would love to take her courage and her indomitable spirit.

00:53:49.240 --> 00:53:52.640
Anna, boy, is she a smart cookie.

00:53:52.240 --> 00:53:55.560
And then Allen's got all the technical skills.

00:53:54.720 --> 00:53:56.760
And he's a team player.

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:01.240
He such a team player that he might actually give the prize away to be nice.

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:06.880
We know they're looking for...

00:54:06.000 --> 00:54:07.520
There's something in all of us.

00:54:06.560 --> 00:54:13.440
But what's that final ingredient that they were looking for?

00:54:14.600 --> 00:54:22.720
I want someone who's, with time, with nurturing, with care, is gonna go on to make cutting-edge wildlife films.

00:54:22.520 --> 00:54:23.640
Who can you bring more out of?

00:54:22.720 --> 00:54:25.840
There's only one job.

00:54:24.960 --> 00:54:26.040
There is only one job.

00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:53.000
The crew that's been with them every step of the way gather to hear the verdict.

00:54:52.160 --> 00:54:55.080
Here we are at the end of our epic adventure.

00:54:55.640 --> 00:55:04.960
We started with nine wildlife enthusiasts.

00:55:04.120 --> 00:55:13.600
But, as you've known all along, there is only one job going... ..at the BBC's natural history unit.

00:55:14.960 --> 00:55:17.680
Cherylin.

00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:26.160
I don't think your film was the best.

00:55:25.200 --> 00:55:31.920
But I think some of your camera work really made the grade.

00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:32.640
(At last. )

00:55:31.960 --> 00:55:34.880
Anna.

00:55:35.280 --> 00:55:44.120
You took a while to emerge as a potential finalist.

00:55:45.840 --> 00:55:50.400
But over the weeks your intuition with the wildlife has become very apparent.

00:55:49.520 --> 00:55:54.000
And you have also shown yourself to be a strong team leader.

00:55:53.200 --> 00:55:55.760
Allen.

00:55:54.880 --> 00:55:59.680
Who is this rugged man I see before me?

00:55:59.640 --> 00:56:02.680
A little bit of a change then?

00:56:02.120 --> 00:56:21.080
Throughout this, your camerawork has been very strong, but behind your gentle and considerate team player, has been this steely determination to realise your dream.

00:56:40.520 --> 00:56:44.400
Welcome to the unit.

00:56:48.120 --> 00:56:49.600
Thank you!

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:08.600
The Masai would like to congratulate you on your success in the Masai Mara.

00:57:18.600 --> 00:57:20.840
I feel elated.

00:57:20.040 --> 00:57:21.640
This is just unreal.

00:57:20.920 --> 00:57:25.120
A chance to work at the NHU is just fab.

00:57:27.120 --> 00:57:30.600
This has been the best experience of my life, yes.

00:57:29.720 --> 00:57:31.880
Definitely.

00:57:30.920 --> 00:57:34.640
The things I've filmed and the things I've done, the people that I've worked with, you can never take that away at all.

00:57:35.520 --> 00:57:39.960
And I'm so going to use it in what I do and in my teaching.

00:57:39.160 --> 00:57:40.880
I really, really will.

00:57:41.760 --> 00:57:43.520
Something happened to me this week.

00:57:42.560 --> 00:57:46.200
I probably found myself, you know.

00:57:45.400 --> 00:57:50.720
I really, really just feel so much more confident and relaxed.

00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:55.760
In a way, I've won as well, so I'm really happy about that.

00:57:58.840 --> 00:58:05.920
When it came down to it, I went for the person who showed the most potential and that, without a doubt in my mind, is Anna.

00:58:06.160 --> 00:58:10.840
The longest and most challenging job interview in the world.

00:58:09.960 --> 00:58:11.400
But I did it.

00:58:10.480 --> 00:58:12.360
I got it.
